WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.860
Tesla finalizes its ai5 processor and restarts the dojo 3 supercomputer using Intel packaging. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 596. Tesla has finalized development of its artificial intelligence 5 automotive processor. Volume production is now scheduled at both TSMC and Samsung sites. The ai5 chip is positioned as offering performance on par with Nvidia's hopper architecture. Two units equal

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:59.840
one Blackwell processor in inference workloads. The company revived the previously halted Dojo 3 supercomputer project. Intel joins as a key packaging partner using EMIB technology for Dojo modules. The approach shifts from prior TSMC reliance and addresses capacity constraints. The Dojo 3 project had been paused earlier due to packaging bottlenecks. EMIB technology allows modular assembly of Dojo compute units without relying solely on

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:27.860
TSMC's advanced packaging lines. The move diversifies Tesla's supply chain for both vehicle inference silicon and training hardware. Early demand signals for the cyber cab are rising after the Austin launch. Tesla is already gauging order demand and preparing for a large order log in coming years. The company is assessing who will place the initial fleet orders. Production aims for one cyber cab unit every 5 seconds on a dedicated high speed line.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:38.800
Tesla has stated that the target manufacturing cadence requires that dedicated line. The unboxed process reduces production line size by 50% while raising output.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:53.120
Separate modules are built in parallel and joined late in assembly molded exterior panels use recycled material and remove the conventional paint shop. The parallel module build reduces the floor space required for final integration.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:02:16.480
Recycled content panels eliminate the need for a traditional paint booth. The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration open an audit into about 1000 Tesla cyber cab vehicles. The probe examines how the EV maker certified compliance with federal safety standards. The audit follows the start of commercial cyber cab rides in limited areas of Austin on September 3rd.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:31.360
The no steering wheel, no pedal robo taxi, drew regulatory scrutiny over its self certification process. The audit focuses on whether the vehicle meets existing federal motor vehicle safety standards written for cargo with conventional controls.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:42.860
Tesla self certified the roughly 1000 units before placing them into the initial Austin service. The agency is now reviewing that certification after the first paid rides began.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:53.760
Texas records show 45 cyber cabs registered for driverless operation as part of the rollout. No official deadline exists for the current FMVSS audit.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:03:07.760
First meaningful signals could appear in one to three months. A substantive outcome is likely in three to nine months. NHTSA is simultaneously rewriting several of the FMVSS rules under review.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:19.000
A clean early safety record will not decide the audit outcome but strengthens Tesla's case. The current Austin fleet has accumulated unsupervised miles without reported issues.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:30.560
Avoiding incidents remains critical to prevent regulators or media from adding reasons to slow deployment. A single avoidable incident could shift the narrative around the self certification approach.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:38.420
Self certification places the burden of proving compliance squarely on the manufacturer before any regulator reviews the design.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:48.180
Tesla has used this path for the cyber cab declaring the vehicle meets federal motor vehicle safety standards even though it lacks a steering wheel pedals and mirrors.

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:57.060
The approach accelerates deployment when the data support it yet it also concentrates risk in a single internal judgment that later audits can revisit.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:03.920
Manufacturers choosing this route must maintain detailed internal records that can withstand later examination.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:14.060
The cyber cabs design departs from decades of assumptions built into the existing standards making the internal certification step more consequential than for conventional vehicles.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:23.060
When an audit begins the original self certification decision becomes the central document under review rather than a starting point for negotiation.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:32.740
The NHTS-A audit now underway tests exactly that judgment against existing standards written for vehicles with conventional controls.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:40.180
Tesla's position rests on its record of unsupervised miles and the absence of incidents in the initial Austin fleet.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:50.360
Regulators must weigh whether those miles constitute sufficient evidence or whether the absence of traditional controls requires new test protocols that do not yet exist.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:05:00.300
The audit process itself does not automatically halt operations but it creates an open question that fleet customers and insurance providers will watch closely.

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:09.200
Tesla has published aggregate safety data from its broader supervised fleet and that data is being referenced in discussions around the new vehicle.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:18.920
The outcome will depend on whether the agency accepts the existing data set as adequate or requests additional validation specific to the no controls configuration.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:31.500
If the audit concludes that current standards cannot accommodate the design, Tesla faces a choice between redesigning hardware or waiting for the agency to finish its ongoing rewrite of the relevant rules.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:38.760
Either path carries direct cost in added engineering time or delayed revenue from scaled robot taxi operations.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:46.100
The outcome will show whether self certification remains a reliable route for vehicles that depart sharply from legacy assumptions.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:54.400
Hardware changes would require recertification and new tooling while waiting for rule updates shifts the timeline for volume production.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:06:04.900
In both cases, the capital already committed to the unboxed manufacturing line remains in place but the pace at which that line can be filled depends on regulatory clarity.

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:10.760
Before we go, the audit timeline and cybercab reduction targets will shape what comes next.

